# TIER 1 - Intrinsic Reaction Coordinate verification of a converged saddle
# (ORCA 6.1). Run this AFTER the OptTS + FREQ run is accepted (exactly one
# imaginary mode showing the correct bond reorganization). Start from the
# converged TS geometry file (e.g. V-TSn_accepted.xyz).
# Purpose: prove that the saddle actually connects the claimed reactant and
# product minima. A saddle without this proof is not a barrier.

! XTB2 IRC

%pal nprocs 3 end

%irc
  InitHess calc_anfreq     # cheap analytic Hessian at the xTB level
  hessMode 0               # mode 0 = the imaginary (reaction) mode
  Direction both           # walk forward and backward from the saddle
  MaxIter 200
end

* xyzfile 0 1 ts_converged.xyz

# After the run:
#   1) ORCA writes *_IRC_F.xyz and *_IRC_B.xyz (last geometry of each walk);
#   2) optimize EACH of those with t1_xTb_opt_freq.inp;
#   3) the two re-optimized structures must reproduce the energies of the
#      claimed reactant and product minima within about 5 kJ/mol;
#   4) record the IRC confirmations in the register alongside the barrier.
